  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe estate tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) Law is a flat rate of 6% on the value of the estate exceeding Five Million Pesos (₱5,000,000).\n\n### Interpretation\nThe estate tax is computed based on the net estate value, which is the gross estate less allowable deductions. The flat rate of 6% applies only to the portion of the estate that exceeds the threshold of ₱5,000,000. This means that estates valued at or below this threshold are exempt from estate tax.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor estate planning and administration, this means that individuals with estates valued at more than ₱5,000,000 should prepare for a 6% tax on the amount exceeding this threshold. Executors and heirs must ensure compliance with filing requirements and payment of the estate tax within the prescribed period to avoid penalties.",
